            </div>
            <div class="intro-copy reveal reveal--late">
                <h2 id="intro-title">What is a whole house water filtration system?</h2>
                <p>A whole house water filtration system, sometimes called a point-of-entry filter, connects to the cold water line where it enters your property. It filters the water before it splits off to the kitchen, bathrooms, laundry and garden. An under-sink or benchtop filter only treats the water from one tap.</p>
                <p>Mains water in Australia is safe to drink. It's treated under the <a class="text-link" href="https://guidelines.nhmrc.gov.au/australian-drinking-water-guidelines/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Australian Drinking Water Guidelines</a>, and chlorine or chloramine is added to keep it safe on the way to your home. The trade-off is a chemical taste and smell, plus that tight, dry feeling after a shower. Older pipes can also add sediment and rust along the way.</p>
                <p>A whole house system deals with all of that at the point of entry. Your water was safe to begin with. It just ends up tasting, smelling and feeling better everywhere in the house.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--stages" aria-labelledby="stages-title">
