                <h2 id="regional-title">Water quality isn't the same everywhere in Australia</h2>
                <p>Melbourne's water is naturally soft, so for most Victorian homes the main issues are chlorine taste and smell, plus sediment in older streets. Adelaide and Perth water tends to be much harder, which makes scale control more important. Homes on rainwater tanks or bores face a different set of risks again.</p>
                <p>That's why we look at your water and your plumbing before we recommend anything.</p>
                
