    <section class="section section--pfas" aria-labelledby="pfas-title">
        
        <div class="section-shell pfas-layout">
            <div class="pfas-copy reveal">
                <h2 id="pfas-title">PFAS in Australian water: what you should know</h2>
                <p>PFAS are a group of man-made chemicals, often called "forever chemicals" because they break down so slowly. In June 2025 the National Health and Medical Research Council (NHMRC) tightened the <a class="text-link text-link--light" href="https://guidelines.nhmrc.gov.au/australian-drinking-water-guidelines/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Australian Drinking Water Guidelines</a>. The limits are now 8 ng/L for PFOS, 30 ng/L for PFHxS and 200 ng/L for PFOA, plus a new value of 1,000 ng/L for PFBS.</p>
                <p>The NHMRC says the vast majority of Australia's drinking water supplies are already below these levels. The higher risk sits with bore water near contaminated sites. If that's your situation, or you'd simply like an extra margin, talk to us about <a class="text-link text-link--light" href="<?php echo $baseUrl; ?>/request-a-quote.php">PFAS-rated filtration</a>.</p>
                
            </div>
            <div class="pfas-panel reveal reveal--late">
                <div class="pfas-panel__head"><span>PFAS</span><span>NHMRC</span></div>
                <dl class="pfas-values">
                    <div><dt>PFOS</dt><dd>8 <small>ng/L</small></dd></div>
                    <div><dt>PFHxS</dt><dd>30 <small>ng/L</small></dd></div>
                    <div><dt>PFOA</dt><dd>200 <small>ng/L</small></dd></div>
                    <div><dt>PFBS</dt><dd>1,000 <small>ng/L</small></dd></div>
                </dl>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

