    <section class="section section--faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
        <div class="section-shell faq-layout">
            <div class="faq-heading reveal"><h2 id="faq-title">Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
            <div class="faq-list reveal reveal--late">
                <article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-1"><span>Q. What does a whole house water filter remove?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-1" hidden><p>The PureLine triple-stage system reduces chlorine by more than 95%, and cuts VOCs and pesticides by more than 90%. It also traps sediment, rust and silt, and reduces chloramines, iron and some heavy metals. It's designed to improve treated mains water rather than make untreated water safe to drink.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-2"><span>Q. Will a whole house filter lower my water pressure?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-2" hidden><p>The system is rated for flows of around 30 litres per minute, which is enough for normal household use. Most homes won't notice a difference. Pressure can drop as cartridges fill up, which is usually the first sign one needs changing.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-3"><span>Q. How often do the filters need changing?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-3" hidden><p>Every 6 to 12 months, depending on your water quality and how much you use. Each cartridge takes about 5 to 10 minutes to swap, and we'll remind you when it's time.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-4"><span>Q. Does it remove fluoride?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-4" hidden><p>No. The standard carbon cartridges aren't designed to remove fluoride. If fluoride removal matters to you, ask us about other options.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-5"><span>Q. Does it soften hard water?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-5" hidden><p>The second stage helps limit limescale, but it isn't a salt-based water softener. In very hard water areas you may need a dedicated softener as well, and we'll tell you at the assessment.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-6"><span>Q. Will it strip the minerals out of my water?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-6" hidden><p>No. Carbon filtration reduces chemicals and particles but leaves dissolved minerals like calcium and magnesium in the water. That's one of the differences between carbon filtration and reverse osmosis.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-7"><span>Q. Do I need a plumber to install it?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-7" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-7" hidden><p>Yes. A whole house filter connects to your main water line, so Australian plumbing rules (AS/NZS 3500) require a licensed plumber. Our installs are all done by licensed plumbers.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-8"><span>Q. How much does a whole house water filter cost?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-8" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-8" hidden><p>It depends on your home, plumbing layout and whether you need extras like a pre-filter. Your assessment is free and the quote is fixed.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-9" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-9"><span>Q. Can it be used with tank or bore water?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-9" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-9" hidden><p> Tank and bore water often need an extra sediment pre-filter, and bore water should be tested first. The standard system is designed for treated mains water, not as a disinfection unit.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-10" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-10"><span>Q. Where is PureLine based?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-10" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-10" hidden><p>Our office is at 46 Palladium Circuit, Clyde North VIC 3978. We service, and our dealer network covers other regions.</p></div>
</article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

